<title>NORWAY: Amoco plugs North Sea exploration well.</title>
<headline>Amoco plugs North Sea exploration well.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Norwegian Oil Directorate (OD) said on Wednesday Amoco Norway had found spore traces of hydrocarbons in exploration well 1/3-8, but no production test had been undertaken before it was permanently plugged.</p>
<p>The exploration well was spudded to a depth of 5,161 metres below sea level, west of the Gyda oilfield in the southern secotr of the Norwegian North Sea.</p>
<p>Amoco was operator of the well, which falls on licence 011 operated by Norske Shell. Norske Conoco is the third partner in the licence.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
